## GRADING (binding; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and words.** A third path, or a changed byte of `DEPLOY.md` outside line 203 = Blocker (STOP: new word); a `!`, a trailing backslash, a second physical line in the check = Major; non-ASCII in an added line, a skip/only = Major; a real organisation, client or person in the test's text = Major; a ticket key in the squash or PR text = Minor (corrected in your files), in a head commit message or a test comment = Note (a test TITLE naming a key = Note); `localdomain` in squash text = Major; a person's name or secret = Blocker; **a false sentence in a commit message, the PR title or the squash text = Minor, Major if about what the line accepts or refuses.**
- **G-2 the line.** A cell the OLD line refuses and the NEW accepts = Blocker, STOP (security-shaped). A flip outside the two named families and the N1 list, or a whole real script or the complete script (+ one blank line) refused = Major. An engine disagreement or error on a cell = Major if it changes a verdict the property names, Minor otherwise (NUL shapes: Note). A false refusal of a shape a real `pg_restore` can write = Major; of a hand-made shape = Note. Round-1 line facts CARRY only as D1-D3 say.
- **G-3 rows and plants.** A new row red or flaky on the head (3 runs, shuffle) = Major; counts other than the claims = Major unless explained; lint, prettier, typecheck, build or unit rc non-zero = Major; a failed set at the head not equal to main's = Major; a removed or weakened assertion not re-asserted = Major; **q3 or q4 leaving every b778 row green = Major (the round-1 holes are not closed: that is a NO GO at the cap)**; a plant of q1-q16 (except a proved-equivalent q8) leaving every row green = Major; a new row that cannot fail (D5 a) = Major; a survivor of your own mutant search: graded by R2-G (D9.4).
- **G-4 sentences.** A NEW `DEPLOY.md` operator sentence FALSE of the line = Major (neighbour class). **B1173-3 is CARRIED: it is not graded again and does not decide this verdict.** INCOMPLETE (`:259`, `:204`) = Note for the product owner; `:263` = Note (PCOMP-117, out).
- **G-5 CodeQL and overlap.** An open alert on the branch = Blocker, STOP; no scan, no CI run = Condition (Tuesday lands only after a clean scan on the PR head); overlap with another open PR on a shared path = Major. **Always Note:** the local-host commit identity; the PR number is not yet known.
- **G-6 verdict (round 2 of 2, the cap).** Any Blocker, or any Major that is not carried (B1173-3) and not a K-1 (the kit's) = **`NO GO (round 2 of 2)`: nothing ships, no landing files, `residue.md` and the findings with their cells are the deliverable, and a third round needs the product owner's word on a card** (G-cap). Only Minor, Note, K-1 and Conditions = `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; none above Note = `GO`. Add ` (conditional: hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN)` while D7 is not "scanned and clean". **Do not soften a Major to reach a GO because this is the cap, and do not harden a Minor to a NO GO because the survivors exist: grade by the rules above and show the table.**

## LOAD (binding; the round-1 kit's LOAD section applies with the renames)
8 cores shared. Heavy = `docker build`, any container run, any vitest run, the awk matrix over many files: **start only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent: say so), recorded beside each result; **one at a time, behind your seat lock `.tools/b1181/lock` AND the project lock `.tools/composer-heavy.lock`** (through your `heavy.sh`). A MOVING heartbeat to `.tools/b1181/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; no `pgrep -f` on your own command line; every command gets `/dev/null` or its input. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b1181-*` containers, networks and images, by exact name. The single-file `awk` runs on one fixture, git reads and `gh` GETs are light and need no lock.

